From 5a6c7985083f1f7c89331f16460a9f0c23f218b8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Z User <z@container>
Date: Sat, 3 Oct 2026 20:22:47 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] ci hardening: binutils provenance binding, declared
 PyYAML, all-or-nothing test channels, structured hosted diagnostics,
 quote-aware comments
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Audit response (8 findings adjudicated; 1H/4M/3L). Every claim was probed
against the merged code before a fix was written; the two where the audit
was wrong are documented in the code instead of "fixed":

- PROVENANCE (the high finding): the ensure_gas_247 fast path accepted ANY
  pair under the install prefix that self-reported an anchored 2.47.*
  token and passed the functional canary — a stale pair from an older
  pin, a pair installed by another tool, a swapped/tampered prefix all
  rode the fast path while the tarball BYTES were pinned, which is a gap
  between "the tarball is pinned" and "this pair came from those bytes".
  Now every verified-tarball build writes <prefix>/.lccc-binutils-provenance
  (target, tarball_version, tarball sha256, and the sha256 of BOTH
  installed binaries) and the fast path requires the marker's recorded
  tarball digest to equal the CURRENT pin (a rotation retires every
  existing cache automatically) and the recorded binary digests to equal
  the installed bytes (a swap, tamper, truncation or partial overwrite
  rebuilds even when the pair still self-reports 2.47 and passes the
  canary). Exact key set; duplicate/unknown/missing keys rebuild. Written
  atomically. Honest boundary documented in the script: a local attacker
  who can write the binaries can rewrite the marker — the runner FS is
  the trusted side; the marker closes every accidental and environmental
  drift case. Self-test 15 -> 26 cases (missing/empty/rotated/swapped/
  tampered/missing-key/extra-key/duplicate/garbage markers), and the
  lookalike-digest case is now constructed by a guaranteed-different
  first-two-hex-digit flip — the old `${sum%??}ff` splice reproduced the
  SAME digest verbatim because the pinned tarball's sha256 ends in "ff",
  making that case silently vacuous (the defect class this matrix hunts).

- DECLARED DEPENDENCY: PyYAML is load-bearing for a required gate on both
  mirrors and was declared nowhere (it worked on hosted runners only as
  an image property). ci.yml installs python3-yaml at the point of first
  use; the checker's ImportError path is now a clean single-message
  failure (no traceback) with distro-correct advice (apt for the system
  python, pip only inside a venv — the old message's pip-into-system-
  python advice is PEP-668-wrong); ci_local.sh's parity gate (the first
  local consumer) carries the requirement note.

- ALL-OR-NOTHING TEST CHANNELS: a partially-set or invalid explicit
  ASMDIFF_TEST_*/ENCDIFF_TEST_OBJDUMP used to be completed silently from
  ambient PATH — a mixed oracle pair (pinned as + distro objdump) is
  exactly what the pin regime refuses. Explicit channels are now never
  completed from PATH; bare mode skips with the reason (and the partial-
  config diagnostic names the MISSING channel — polarity pinned by test),
  require mode errors as before. New resolver test classes: 5 cases in
  test_asmdiff, 4 in test_encdiff, all matrix cells (partial/invalid/
  valid x bare/require).

- STRUCTURED HOSTED DIAGNOSTICS: hosted violations said "hosted line 742"
  — a line number into a synthetic concatenation of every workflow's
  bodies. Every hosted diagnostic now carries the workflow file, job id,
  step name and body line (GitHub's own addressing). The records
  interface also checks hosted bodies STEP BY STEP — every run: block is
  its own shell, and the joined form let a trailing continuation at the
  end of one step swallow the first line of the next (over-join fixed;
  the plain-string interface the mutation tests drive is preserved).

- QUOTE-AWARE COMMENTS: the `re.search(r"\s#", line)` cut truncated any
  hosted line carrying a double-quoted " # " — the remnant had an
  unbalanced quote, shlex refused it, and _logical_command_lines DROPPED
  it: a contracted invocation with a quoted-# argument silently escaped
  the universal contract check. _cut_shell_comment tracks quote state
  (and double-quote backslash escapes); used for hosted run bodies AND
  the local side of check_hosted_steps_mirrored.

- TRIGGER POLICY DOCUMENTED: why pull_request_target (secrets-bearing,
  runs from the BASE ref — never sees the patch) and merge_group (only
  when branch protection queues a merge, which this repo's protection
  does not require) are deliberately not coverage events, and what
  adding merge_group would mean (a contract change, not a spelling).

- Single-file architecture KEPT deliberately (module map added to the
  docstring: the whole trust model readable top-to-bottom, flat-scripts
  repo convention, import-audit gates); the "split into modules" advice
  was declined with reasons, not silently.

Validated: checker PASS on the real tree (134 commands, 12 contracts);
mutation suite 66/66 (60 + 6 new; both new guards deletion-proven —
neutralizing the quote-aware cutter or the step-addressed diagnostics
fails exactly their tests); ensure_gas self-test 26/26; test_asmdiff 28/28
and test_encdiff 73/73 each bare AND pinned+require; missing-PyYAML path
proven clean (rc=1, actionable message, no traceback); bash -n both shell
files; workflow-shell + script-imports green.
